# Docs and technology

## Authoritative documentation

Treat `/docs` as the product specification. Prefer these over ad-hoc assumptions:

- `docs/BUSINESS_REQUIREMENTS_DOCUMENT.md`
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE_DOCUMENTS.md`
- `docs/DATABASE_DOCUMENTATION.md`
- `docs/API_DOCUMENTATION.md`
- `docs/SECURITY_GUIDE.md`
- `docs/DEVELOPMENT_ROADMAP.md`

Also honor `PRODUCTION_READINESS.md` and `docs/ADR_001_TENANCY.md` (shared-schema + `tenant_id` for MVP).

## Technology stack

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Backend | FastAPI |
| ORM | SQLAlchemy 2.x |
| Database | PostgreSQL |
| Frontend | Next.js / React |
| Cache | Redis |
| Tasks | Celery / RabbitMQ |
| Containers | Docker |

Schema changes require versioned **Alembic** migrations. Never manually alter production schemas.
